    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d267-a3">

                <pb facs="0765" n="551" sameAs="frus:frus1871/pg551"/>

                <head>No. 3, (with dispatch No. 98.)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of Foreign Affairs</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Honolulu</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1871-01-24"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 24, 1871.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> In answer to your letter of the 17th
                    instant, and in accordance with your request therein made, I am directed to
                    inclose herewith an account of the items of expenditure ($2,965) incurred for
                    the voyage of the Kilauea, approved by the minister of the interior.</p>
                <p>Hoping that the same will be satisfactory, I have the honor to be, with the
                    highest respect, sir, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WM. JARRETT, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry A. Peirce, Minister Resident
                            of the United States.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
